# This repository has mixed line endings, on purpose-of-record rather than by
# design: engine/vg/api/*.py, web/src/services/*.ts, web/src/types.ts and
# STATUS.md are CRLF; most other files are LF.
#
# `* -text` tells git to store and check out every file exactly as it is, on
# every machine, and to convert nothing. That is deliberate. Normalising to LF
# would be tidier, but it would rewrite roughly 560 files in one commit and
# make every line of the project's history look changed on the same day.
#
# The practical consequence for editors, spelt out in AGENTS.md: a script that
# reads a file as text and writes it back rewrites every ending and turns a
# six-line change into a whole-file diff. Read and write bytes, or check
# `b"\r\n" in path.read_bytes()` first. `git diff --stat` catches it.
* -text

# Binary, so git never tries to diff or merge them.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.pt   binary
*.pth  binary
*.onnx binary
*.engine binary
*.xlsx binary
*.zip  binary
